# 2 Carat Radiant Cut Diamond Ring: Lab Wins at 8×.

A 2 carat radiant cut diamond ring is a genuine statement purchase. At this weight the stone is 8.1×6.0mm face-up — wide enough to command the hand from across the room. The only question that matters is whether you are paying natural prices or lab prices to get there.

This guide gives you every combination: lab and natural stones, multiple settings, all metals, and complete ring totals from certified market data. The 2ct Credibility Line and the Natural Price Cliff will tell you exactly who this upgrade is for.

Every price on this page is stone plus setting. Every table has a "What this means" column.

**TL;DR:**
- → **For lab buyers: yes, unequivocally** — 2ct lab ring from $3,029. D-IF in white gold under $5,200. No other shape delivers this at 2ct.
- → **For natural buyers: only with eyes open** — 2ct natural ring starts at $18,574. That is 2.2× more than the 1.5ct natural entry. You are buying rarity, not just size.
- 2 carat radiant cut diamond rings from [$3,029 lab](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?ShapeID=Radiant&ct=1.9-2.09&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) or [$18,574 natural](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/16750163?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
- → Best lab pick: [2ct E-VVS1 IGI $2,220](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/26351307?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$3,080**
- → Best natural entry: [2ct D-VS2 GIA $17,714](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/16750163?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ten Prong WG $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$18,574**
- Contrarian truth: G color is correct for natural 2ct radiant — not D or E. Color concentrates less in a radiant than in a step cut, and G saves you thousands with zero visual penalty in a prong setting.
- → See the [Natural Price Cliff chart](#the-natural-price-cliff) and the [2ct vs 1.5ct comparison](#2ct-vs-15ct-radiant-cut) below.

